{"id":877,"date":"2020-11-10T14:00:06","date_gmt":"2020-11-10T22:00:06","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=877"},"modified":"2024-09-01T20:07:42","modified_gmt":"2024-09-02T03:07:42","slug":"codrone-arduino-installing-software","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-installing-software\/","title":{"rendered":"Installing Software"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a4a7f91\" name=\"6a2215a4a7f91\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Software installation video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>Check out the video, or follow the steps below to get Arduino installed on your computer.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=wdcfL6O4mqs&amp;feature=emb_logo&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a4a80d3\" name=\"6a2215a4a80d3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Installing Arduino<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Arduino is open source, which means anyone (including you) can download and use it for freeeeeeee! To download and install, go to the\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.arduino.cc\/en\/Main\/Software\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arduino website<\/a>, select the best package for your operating system, and then download. <strong>PLEASE NOTE:<\/strong> <strong>The Arduino Web Editor is not compatible with the CoDrone Pro<\/strong> since you cannot select the Rokit board used to upload programs to the CoDrone Pro.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;878&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a4a8141\" name=\"6a2215a4a8141\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Install<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>When the download is finished, open and run the downloaded installer.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;879&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;880&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a4a8197\" name=\"6a2215a4a8197\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Selecting packages<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Select all of the components! You don&#8217;t have to check all of the shortcuts they suggest, but we recommend creating at least one to make your life easier.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;881&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a4a81e8\" name=\"6a2215a4a81e8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Finish installing<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Select install to start installation to the default folder.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;882&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Once Arduino is finished installing, hit close and you should have an Arduino icon on your desktop or in your start menu![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;883&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a4a8237\" name=\"6a2215a4a8237\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Installing CoDrone library<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Robolink created a lot of CoDrone functions and put them all in the CoDrone library in Arduino. If you want to use them, you need to install the CoDrone library through the Arduino Library Manager.<\/p>\n<p>First, open Arduino and go to Sketch &gt; Include Library &gt; Manage Libraries.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;884&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a4a8294\" name=\"6a2215a4a8294\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Library Manager<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>A Library Manager dialog box should appear. Filter your search by typing CoDrone in the search box.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;887&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a4a82e5\" name=\"6a2215a4a82e5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Installing CoDrone Library<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You should see CoDrone by Robolink in the search results.\u00a0If you don&#8217;t see the CoDrone library, it&#8217;s probably time to\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.arduino.cc\/en\/Main\/Software\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">update your Arduino IDE.<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Next, select the library and click the Install button![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;888&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a4a8339\" name=\"6a2215a4a8339\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Confirm installation<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>You should see INSTALLED next to the library. Remember to\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/basecamp.robolink.com\/cwists\/567\/href\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">update your libraries<\/a> often!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;889&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 10 Software installation video [vc_column_text] Check out the video, or follow the steps below to get Arduino installed on your computer. [\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=wdcfL6O4mqs&amp;feature=emb_logo\" align=\"center\"] [\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 Installing&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-installing-software\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1752,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":804,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2163,2164,2165,2177,2170,2169],"class_list":["post-877","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-pro","lesson-tag-getting-started","lesson-tag-installation","lesson-tag-software","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/877","target